00:16:02,713 --> 00:16:06,700
I remember them working like animals
in the fields, covered in dirt.

262
00:16:08,400 --> 00:16:13,237
Finally, after ten years, they managed
to make this sandy soil usable.

263
00:16:13,320 --> 00:16:14,700
It was an amazing

264
00:16:23,120 --> 00:16:28,737
Accomplishment then about 15 years ago
your father showed up and stole the land.

265
00:16:28,820 --> 00:16:34,037
Those good people sweated blood to plow
he earned the name Grim Reaper Bostock.

266
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:38,277
When he slaughtered them
all at this point line would

267
00:16:38,360 --> 00:16:41,540
accomplish nothing we We
don't care about the money.

268
00:16:41,780 --> 00:16:44,015
Whatever happens, I will not run away.

269
00:16:44,320 --> 00:16:48,120
However, I will take revenge
for what happened 15 years ago.

270
00:16:48,520 --> 00:16:49,800
Mark my words.

271
00:16:54,240 --> 00:16:56,946
It's impossible to forget
something like that.

272
00:16:59,580 --> 00:17:01,060
Huh? What's happening?

273
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:04,280
What the hell?

274
00:17:04,660 --> 00:17:05,900
Hey, don't you worry.

275
00:17:06,100 --> 00:17:07,806
We'll get you some help, pal.

276
00:17:12,440 --> 00:17:15,060
Am I gonna die?

277
00:17:15,460 --> 00:17:16,497
No, it's all right.

278
00:17:16,580 --> 00:17:17,477
You're gonna be okay.

279
00:17:17,560 --> 00:17:19,442
The bullet passed right through.

280
00:17:20,460 --> 00:17:21,290
Attention!

281
00:17:21,373 --> 00:17:24,496
I will now discuss the demands
on behalf of these men.

282
00:17:29,280 --> 00:17:30,120
You're going?

283
00:17:31,320 --> 00:17:33,080
He has my oldest daughter.

284
00:17:33,360 --> 00:17:34,713
I have no other choice.

285
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:35,917
But hear this, Stan.

286
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:39,824
When all of this is over, I will
hold you personally responsible.

287
00:17:41,300 --> 00:17:44,535
He was feared fifteen years
ago as Grim Reaper Bostock.

288
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:49,772
Amazing how the love of a daughter in
the passage of time can change a man.

289
00:18:05,340 --> 00:18:06,928
You have what you want now.

290
00:18:07,140 --> 00:18:09,037
It's time to release the girl, Ingwe.

291
00:18:09,120 --> 00:18:11,649
Please forgive me for
what I'm about to do.

292
00:18:13,800 --> 00:18:17,329
It's not an easy thing to escape
from a past you can't bury.

293
00:18:19,600 --> 00:18:21,280
You can't look away anymore.

294
00:18:21,560 --> 00:18:24,077
It's time you face the
truth about your father.

295
00:18:24,160 --> 00:18:26,757
You can no longer remain ignorant
of the hopes of the people

296
00:18:26,840 --> 00:18:29,917
because of the terrible lie
your entire life was built upon.

297
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:31,360
I am aware of that.

298
00:18:31,520 --> 00:18:32,860
I am aware of that.

299
00:18:34,120 --> 00:18:38,708
But, even if it is true that he was
responsible for all those horrible things,

300
00:18:38,860 --> 00:18:40,520
he is still my daddy.

301
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:43,777
No matter how disobedient
or selfish I was growing up,

302
00:18:43,860 --> 00:18:47,154
he was always a warm, dedicated
and loving father to me.

303
00:19:23,740 --> 00:19:24,570
Father!

304
00:19:24,780 --> 00:19:26,020
Father, I'm coming!

305
00:19:26,560 --> 00:19:29,180
Daddy, hold on! Daddy! Daddy!

306
00:19:29,540 --> 00:19:30,617
Please, Daddy, no!

307
00:19:30,700 --> 00:19:32,960
I'm I'm all right, honey.

308
00:19:33,260 --> 00:19:34,700
It's only my shoulder.

309
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:42,529
What are you crying about?

310
00:19:44,360 --> 00:19:47,301
Listen, I don't want you
thanking me for anything.

311
00:19:47,460 --> 00:19:50,578
I just simply got distracted
and it threw my aim off.

312
00:19:50,700 --> 00:19:51,530
That's all

313
00:19:53,740 --> 00:19:55,622
Can't believe he's really crying

314
00:19:56,740 --> 00:19:57,640
See you later.

315
00:19:57,780 --> 00:19:58,897
I'm turning myself in.

316
00:19:58,980 --> 00:19:59,810
Whoa there.

317
00:20:00,020 --> 00:20:01,844
It's too soon for the epilogue.

318
00:20:02,920 --> 00:20:04,220
It's all over, Stan.

319
00:20:04,400 --> 00:20:06,500
I'm gonna give myself up. Not yet.

320
00:20:06,720 --> 00:20:09,160
I still need you to resist me. What?

321
00:20:09,860 --> 00:20:12,997
I never dreamed that I would be
presented with such an opportunity.

322
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:15,180
I can see the headlines now.

323
00:20:15,540 --> 00:20:17,680
Besieged criminal kills Mr. Bostock.

324
00:20:17,860 --> 00:20:21,037
Sheriff forced to shoot culprit
down as he attempts to resist.

325
