It makes for a pretty article.

326
00:20:22,900 --> 00:20:25,400
A real showpiece for my scrapbook.

327
00:20:26,140 --> 00:20:27,080
No, Stan.

328
00:20:27,840 --> 00:20:29,777
The sheriff is a position of honor.

329
00:20:29,860 --> 00:20:31,017
How could you do this?

330
00:20:31,100 --> 00:20:34,477
Fifteen years ago, this man
stole every right to this town.

331
00:20:34,560 --> 00:20:36,357
I should have been just as powerful.

332
00:20:36,440 --> 00:20:38,616
Yet I was stuck as the lowly sheriff.

333
00:20:38,820 --> 00:20:42,960
I think I'm way past due to receive
a little glory around these parts.

334
00:20:43,320 --> 00:20:44,520
You were in on it.

335
00:20:45,040 --> 00:20:46,200
You're a fiend.

336
00:20:46,380 --> 00:20:47,498
You're a scoundrel.

337
00:20:47,760 --> 00:20:49,760
Throw down your weapons right now.

338
00:20:53,220 --> 00:20:55,300
You unarmed stray dogs.

339
00:20:55,500 --> 00:20:57,320
How grand to be superior.

340
00:21:03,540 --> 00:21:04,920
I have one question.

341
00:21:05,580 --> 00:21:09,457
Tell me, how does it feel to kill
unarmed innocent people like that?

342
00:21:09,540 --> 00:21:11,297
And I have a question for you.

343
00:21:11,380 --> 00:21:13,737
Do you feel anything when
you burn your garbage?

344
00:21:13,820 --> 00:21:15,620
Nifty answer. Sorry I asked.

345
00:21:30,660 --> 00:21:31,900
What? What the?

346
00:21:33,280 --> 00:21:34,320
That was awesome!

347
00:21:34,820 --> 00:21:36,657
