Well, what do you think, Sheriff?

355
00:21:55,280 --> 00:21:58,574
How does it feel to be at the
mercy of a stray dog, huh?

356
00:22:05,760 --> 00:22:07,440
You can relax, Sheriff.

357
00:22:07,680 --> 00:22:09,209
I'm not going to kill you.

358
00:22:10,080 --> 00:22:10,962
However, you...

359
00:22:16,320 --> 00:22:18,614
No longer have the right to be Sheriff.

360
00:22:19,940 --> 00:22:22,337
Wanna know something interesting, Sheriff?

361
00:22:22,420 --> 00:22:24,997
Repeat carefully after me Okay,

362
00:23:18,440 --> 00:23:19,980
Thank you.

363
00:23:45,540 --> 00:23:46,370
Oh,

364
00:23:46,453 --> 00:23:48,457
I'll see you, I'll see you,

365
00:23:48,540 --> 00:23:50,957
I'll see you,

366
00:23:51,040 --> 00:23:51,897
I'll

367
00:23:51,980 --> 00:23:58,980
see

368
00:23:59,360 --> 00:24:00,190
you.

369
00:24:13,660 --> 00:24:15,484
What is lost will never return.

370
00:24:16,320 --> 00:24:18,900
Important things, irreplaceable things.

371
00:24:19,520 --> 00:24:24,217
But what is needed to keep those things is
in the firm will, packed into one bullet.

372
00:24:24,300 --> 00:24:28,040
Man knows, he knows that nothing
will begin unless he speaks.

373
00:24:28,700 --> 00:24:31,960
And that nothing will
change unless he moves.
